      "text": "Given the system of equations:\n1. \\( A + 2 = B - 2 = C \\times 2 = D \\div 2 \\)\n2. \\( A + B + C + D = 36 \\)\n\nLet's denote the common value by \\( k \\). So we can rewrite the equations as:\n1. \\( A = k - 2 \\)\n2. \\( B = k + 2 \\)\n3. \\( C = \\frac{k}{2} \\)\n4. \\( D = 2k \\)\n\nSubstitute these expressions into the sum equation:\n\\[ (k - 2) + (k + 2) + \\frac{k}{2} + 2k = 36 \\]\n\nSimplify the left side:\n\\[ k - 2 + k + 2 + \\frac{k}{2} + 2k = 36 \\]\n\\[ 4k + \\frac{k}{2} = 36 \\]\n\nCombine the terms:\n\\[ \\frac{8k}{2} + \\frac{k}{2} = 36 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{9k}{2} = 36 \\]\n\nSolve for \\( k \\):\n\\[ 9k = 72 \\]\n\\[ k = 8 \\]\n\nNow substitute \\( k = 8 \\) back into the expressions for \\( A \\), \\( B \\), \\( C \\), and \\( D \\):\n\\[ A = 8 - 2 = 6 \\]\n\\[ B = 8 + 2 = 10 \\]\n\\[ C = \\frac{8}{2} = 4 \\]\n\\[ D = 2 \\times 8 = 16 \\]\n\nFinally, calculate the product \\( A \\times B \\times C \\times D \\):\n\\[ A \\times B \\times C \\times D = 6 \\times 10 \\times 4 \\times 16 \\]\n\nLet's compute the product step by step:\n\\[ 6 \\times 10 = 60 \\]\n\\[ 4 \\times 16 = 64 \\]\n\\[ 60 \\times 64 = 3840 \\]\n\nThus, the value of the product \\( A \\times B \\times C \\times D \\) is \\(\\boxed{3840}\\).",
