      "text": "To solve the problem, let's first define the variables and the relationships given:\n\n1. Let \\( x \\) be the common value of the expressions \\( A+2 \\), \\( B-2 \\), \\( C \\times 2 \\), and \\( D \\div 2 \\).\n2. Therefore, we can write:\n   \\[\n   A + 2 = x\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   B - 2 = x\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   C \\times 2 = x\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   D \\div 2 = x\n   \\]\n3. From these equations, we can express \\( A \\), \\( B \\), \\( C \\), and \\( D \\) in terms of \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   A = x - 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   B = x + 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   C = \\frac{x}{2}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   D = 2x\n   \\]\n4. We are given that the sum of these integers is 36:\n   \\[\n   A + B + C + D = 36\n   \\]\n5. Substitute the expressions for \\( A \\), \\( B \\), \\( C \\), and \\( D \\) into the sum equation:\n   \\[\n   (x - 2) + (x + 2) + \\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right) + 2x = 36\n   \\]\n6. Simplify the equation:\n   \\[\n   x - 2 + x + 2 + \\frac{x}{2} + 2x = 36\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4x + \\frac{x}{2} = 36\n   \\]\n7. Combine the terms involving \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{8x}{2} + \\frac{x}{2} = 36\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{9x}{2} = 36\n   \\]\n8. Solve for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   9x = 72\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = 8\n   \\]\n9. Now, substitute \\( x = 8 \\) back into the expressions for \\( A \\), \\( B \\), \\( C \\), and \\( D \\):\n   \\[\n   A = x - 2 = 8 - 2 = 6\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   B = x + 2 = 8 + 2 = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   C = \\frac{x}{2} = \\frac{8}{2} = 4\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   D = 2x = 2 \\times 8 = 16\n   \\]\n10. Calculate the product \\( A \\times B \\times C \\times D \\):\n    \\[\n    A \\times B \\times C \\times D = 6 \\times 10 \\times 4 \\times 16\n    \\]\n11. Perform the multiplication step-by-step:\n    \\[\n    6 \\times 10 = 60\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    60 \\times 4 = 240\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    240 \\times 16 = 3840\n    \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the product \\( A \\times B \\times C \\times D \\) is \\(\\boxed{3840}\\).",
